    {
      "id": "PR64_OTA_MISSING_CORE_IDENTITY_FIELDS_FAIL_OPEN",
      "severity": "P1",
      "status": "open",
      "locations": [
        "_lib/assurance/state-models/models.mjs:371",
        "_lib/assurance/state-models/models.mjs:372",
        "_lib/assurance/state-models/models.mjs:378",
        "_lib/assurance/state-models/models.mjs:385",
        "_lib/assurance/state-models/models.mjs:387",
        "tests/assurance/models/escaped-defects.test.mjs:58",
        "tests/assurance/models/escaped-defects.test.mjs:61"
      ],
      "evidence": "The new identity contract correctly requires buildId, packageId, signedArtifactId, build source, targetBuildId, updateId, group, update source, and capability arrays. It compares platform, environment, runtime, channel, and nativeDigest, but validBuild and validUpdate do not require those five fields to exist. Independent adversarial cases removed the same one of those fields from both build and update. In all five cases the build installed, the update activated, activationRejected stayed zero, and violations remained empty because undefined equaled undefined.",
      "impact": "MODEL_CLEAR can represent an update with no platform, environment, runtime, channel, or native capability digest. Those are mandatory compatibility identities in the requested OTA/build invariant, so equality of missing evidence is a false pass and can admit an update whose native compatibility is unproved.",
      "requiredResolution": "Require nonempty platform, environment, runtime, channel, and nativeDigest in both validBuild and validUpdate, preferably constrain platform/environment to their declared enumerations, add missing-field adversarial cases for build, activation, rollback target, and rollback, and prove each fails closed. Retain the new-source positive witness and all mismatch/identity/rollback negatives.",
      "blocksMerge": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PR64_INVARIANT_DETECTOR_HISTORICAL_COVERAGE_REMAINS_PARTIAL",
      "severity": "P2",
      "status": "open",
      "locations": [
        "_lib/assurance/state-models/models.mjs:622",
        "_lib/assurance/state-models/models.mjs:626",
        "_lib/assurance/state-models/models.mjs:627",
        "_lib/assurance/state-models/models.mjs:688",
        "_lib/assurance/state-models/models.mjs:689",
        "_lib/assurance/state-models/models.mjs:690",
        "_lib/assurance/state-models/models.mjs:721"
      ],
      "evidence": "All 22 present fixtures detect their historical variant and pass the fixed model. Several explicit detector branches still have no targeted historical/fixed fixture, including LiveKit duplicate room/track, fixture-as-real pass, terminal cleanup, and migration deployed-body rewrite, RLS/FORCE RLS loss, and broad grant.",
      "impact": "Property runs prove reachable fixed states, but those fixed transitions cannot create the forbidden states. Removing or inverting the named detector branches would not necessarily fail the historical fixture corpus before PR E mutation enforcement exists.",
      "requiredResolution": "Add minimized historical variants and fixed-model regressions for the named detector branches, or bind equivalent killed mutants before claiming reusable escaped-defect coverage for those branches.",
